# Token Efficiency (always apply)

## Discovery limits
- Never scan `node_modules`, `.venv*`, `target/`, `dist/`, `build/`, `uploads/`, `pages/`, logs, binaries, model weights, or lockfiles.
- No repository-wide `find`, `grep`, or `glob` unless the user explicitly requests a full audit.
- Prefer `Grep` with `path` + `glob` over broad semantic search or exploratory subagents.
- Ask before reading more than **5 files** in one turn; list planned paths first.
- Do not re-read files already in this conversation unless they changed or the edit failed.

## Edit discipline
- Minimal diff only — patch changed lines; never rewrite whole files when a small edit suffices.
- No drive-by refactors, comments, or formatting outside the requested scope.
- No new files (tests, docs, configs) unless requested.
- Match existing naming, imports, and patterns in the touched module.

## Context loading
- Start from user `@file` refs, open tabs, or one entrypoint (`main.py`, `Application.java`, `page.tsx`).
- Trace imports one hop at a time; stop when the call chain is clear.
- For multi-file edits: declare target files upfront, batch reads, no speculative exploration.

## Response discipline
- Concise answers; cite code with `startLine:endLine:path` only when relevant.
- Run commands only when needed to verify or implement.
